    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The pipeline starts with a complete draft, then diagnoses actual lead-time losses, develops a prioritized strategy, and subjects it to specialized certified-quality and warranty-risk scrutiny. A refiner integrates those findings into one plan before the feasibility gate assesses the complete output. If the gate outputs revise, execution returns to the refiner for correction; if it outputs pass, the plan proceeds to the final polisher. The flow is Builder → Analyst → Strategist → Quality Expert → Refiner → Quality Gate, with revise looping to the Refiner, then Polisher."
}
